From: wangzlei <66336933+wangzlei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:31:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] aws-lambda: Lambda Invoke spans in the AWS SDK payload
 extraction

Upstream's AWS payload extraction (payload_extraction.http.aws) recognises S3
and SQS only; a Lambda Invoke call from any AWS SDK stays a plain
"POST /2015-03-31/functions/<fn>/invocations" HTTP client span.

This patch adds a third AWS parser, AWSLambdaSpan (pkg/ebpf/common/http/
aws_lambda.go), next to aws_s3.go / aws_sqs.go and wired the same way
(HTTPSubtypeAWSLambda, request.AWS.Lambda, span name, span getters, tracesgen):
- matched by POST + the exact Invoke path + an AWS request id
  (x-amzn-RequestId) in the response; other Lambda APIs (GetFunction,
  InvokeAsync, InvokeWithResponseStream, ...) are not matched;
- FunctionName forms: name, name:qualifier, partial ARN
  (<account>:function:<name>[:qualifier]) and full ARN (any partition),
  percent-encoded or not; ?Qualifier= wins over an inline qualifier;
- span name "lambda.Invoke" (upstream convention: s3.<Op>, sqs.<Op>);
- attributes: rpc.system.name=aws-api, rpc.method=Lambda/Invoke (fully
  qualified like S3's "S3/<Op>", semconv v1.41 has no rpc.service),
  cloud.region (from the endpoint host), aws.request_id,
  faas.invoked_name (bare function name, also for ARNs),
  faas.invoked_provider=aws, faas.invoked_region (from a full ARN, else the
  endpoint region), error.type on failures;
- errors: a function error is HTTP 200 + x-amz-function-error; the span gets
  status ERROR, the runtime's errorMessage as status message and its
  errorType (fallback: the header value) as error.type. Service errors
  (4xx/5xx) keep the HTTP status handling and get error.type from
  x-amzn-ErrorType (e.g. ResourceNotFoundException).

Go (aws-sdk-go-v2 talks HTTP/2 to Lambda): the request is rebuilt from HTTP/2
frames with the peer IP as Host and the Go probe's URL.Path copy (at most
k_path_max_len = 100 bytes). So the region falls back to the host the Go probe
reported (Request.Host / URL.Host) when the request Host is not an AWS
endpoint, and a path cut short inside "/invocations" (full ARN + long name) is
still accepted once the FunctionName segment is complete and at least "/i"
follows (no other POST /2015-03-31/functions/<name>/... API starts with it).
Known gap: Go async invocations (InvocationType=Event, HTTP/2 202 with an
empty body) stay plain HTTP spans, because upstream's HTTP/2 response
extraction ignores responses without a body.

Lambda is tried before S3 because the S3 parser accepts any request that
carries S3-style request-id headers, while Lambda is matched by its exact path.
Userspace only (the request/response are already in the large HTTP buffer):
no BPF change. Needs the same config as S3/SQS: ebpf.buffer_sizes.http > 0 and
ebpf.payload_extraction.http.aws.enabled: true.

Why upstream does not do it: upstream only implemented S3 and SQS.

Turn it off: payload_extraction.http.aws.enabled: false (disables S3/SQS too),
or drop this patch.

Adot-Obi-Patch: 07-aws-lambda
